{% comment %}
  "Social video carousel" section (homepage section 09 in the client's Figma, "Social — video
  carousel"). Section-local `video_tile` blocks (a Horizon section can't read theme-block
  settings - iterating `section.blocks` for `@theme` blocks gives back empty settings - so
  this mirrors sections/review-cards.liquid: block settings live directly in this section's
  schema and are read straight off `block.settings` in a `for block in section.blocks` loop).

  Each tile is rendered once through snippets/video-tile.liquid, its markup captured, then
  reused in two Horizon slideshows - a desktop one (tiles sized to a fixed `--video-carousel-
  card-width`, see the Desktop grid paragraph below, peeking past the visible count when
  `bleed_right` is on) and a mobile one (single tile at `mobile_card_size`% of the viewport) -
  only one of the pair is visible at a time (hidden--mobile / hidden--desktop), the same
  technique review-cards uses for its own desktop/mobile split.

  Nav arrows: the Figma puts the two 56px arrow buttons in the HEADER, to the right of the
  heading - never overlaid on the tiles - so this can't use the usual `render 'slideshow-
  arrows'` overlay (which renders inside the slideshow's own tree, on top of the media). The
  header buttons here are plain markup, wired straight to the desktop `<slideshow-component>`
  by DOM id: `on:click="#id/previous"` resolves via `document.querySelector` (see assets/
  component.js's declarative event dispatch), which works from anywhere in the document, not
  only from inside the component's own subtree - unlike the ref-less `on:click="/previous"`
  used elsewhere, which requires the button to be a descendant of the component. Because the
  header buttons live outside the slideshow, they can coexist with the progress bar under the
  row - unlike review-cards, where 'progress' and arrows are mutually exclusive, this section
  lets them show together (icons_style: 'progress' + hide_arrows off), matching how
  sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid also shows a progress bar and arrows at once (there,
  side-by-side; here, arrows in the header and the bar below the row).

  Desktop grid: with `desktop_layout: 'auto'` (default) a row whose tile count fits within
  `columns` renders a contained grid instead of the carousel above (`is_desktop_grid` below)
  - `bleed_right` is ignored in that state, since bleeding past the content column only makes
  sense once there's real overflow to scroll into (exactly 4 tiles at columns: 4 otherwise
  bleeds with nothing to scroll, the same clipping bug sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid had
  with a 4-product tab). The header nav arrows above need no extra handling for this: they're
  already gated on `desktop_has_controls` (`card_count > columns`), which is false whenever
  the grid branch is - `desktop_layout: 'carousel'` opts back into always-carousel regardless
  of tile count. Each tile is still captured once via `tile_html` and reused as either a
  slideshow-slide's children (carousel) or a plain grid-item's children (grid). Mobile is
  unaffected either way - `columns` tiles always overflow a phone, so it stays a carousel.

  Card width: both branches size a tile from the SAME `--video-carousel-card-width` custom
  property (set on the outer .video-carousel div, computed from `columns`/`card_gap`) instead
  of each computing its own width independently - the carousel used to derive `--slide-width`
  as a `100%`-based fraction of its OWN (force-full-width, viewport-ish) box, which doesn't
  match the grid's content-column-based math, so a tile visibly resized when the row switched
  from grid to carousel (e.g. adding a 5th tile). The shared variable is built from `--page-
  content-width`/`--page-margin`/`100vw`, NOT assets/base.css's own `--full-page-grid-central-
  column-width` - that one LOOKS like the right tool (it's already the theme's content-column
  width), but verified via getComputedStyle probes to resolve incorrectly (a real 274px
  instead of 294px at 1440) once read through a nested var()-in-calc() chain and finally
  consumed by a property on a box nested deep inside a force-full-width ancestor, rather than
  the .section element it's declared on. See sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid for the same
  fix, reasoning, and verification detail.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_count = section.blocks.size
  assign columns = section.settings.columns | default: 4

  # Known before the tile loop runs (card_count and columns are both section-level, no
  # per-tile dependency) so the loop below can build only the desktop markup that will
  # actually render - see the comment above and sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid, which
  # gained this same auto/grid choice for the same reason (a row that doesn't overflow
  # shouldn't render as a bled carousel with a near-empty progress bar).
  assign desktop_layout = section.settings.desktop_layout | default: 'auto'
  assign is_desktop_grid = false
  if desktop_layout == 'auto' and card_count <= columns
    assign is_desktop_grid = true
  endif

  assign desktop_slides = ''
  assign desktop_grid_items = ''
  assign mobile_slides = ''
-%}

{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- capture tile_html -%}
    {%- render 'video-tile',
      video: block.settings.video,
      video_url: block.settings.video_url,
      poster: block.settings.poster,
      duration: block.settings.duration,
      alt: block.settings.alt,
      image_ratio: section.settings.image_ratio,
      card_radius: section.settings.card_radius,
      block_attributes: block.shopify_attributes
    -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture mobile_slide -%}
    {%- render 'slideshow-slide', index: forloop.index0, children: tile_html, class: 'video-carousel__slide video-carousel__mobile-slide' -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign mobile_slides = mobile_slides | append: mobile_slide -%}

  {%- if is_desktop_grid -%}
    {%- capture grid_item -%}
      <div class="video-carousel__grid-item">{{ tile_html }}</div>
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign desktop_grid_items = desktop_grid_items | append: grid_item -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- capture desktop_slide -%}
      {%- render 'slideshow-slide', index: forloop.index0, children: tile_html, class: 'video-carousel__slide' -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign desktop_slides = desktop_slides | append: desktop_slide -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_gap = section.settings.card_gap | default: 24
  assign mobile_card_size = section.settings.mobile_card_size | default: 70
  assign bleed_right = section.settings.bleed_right

  # A single shared card-width variable (set on the outer .video-carousel div below, and
  # used by both the carousel slide width here and the grid track width in the stylesheet)
  # replaces this rail's old percentage-based --slide-width formula. That formula read
  # `100%` against whichever element it was applied to - inside the force-full-width
  # .video-carousel__desktop (bleed_right on), that resolved against the full bled width,
  # not the 1248px content column the grid uses, so a tile visibly resized switching between
  # a grid tab and a carousel tab (the same bug sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid had with
  # its hard-coded 320px carousel card vs. its ~294px grid card). See the comment on
  # --video-carousel-card-width below (near the .video-carousel div's style attribute) for
  # why it's built from --page-content-width/--page-margin/100vw rather than the theme's
  # own --full-page-grid-central-column-width, which measured unreliably once consumed this
  # deep in a force-full-width tree.
  assign desktop_style = '--slideshow-gap: ' | append: card_gap | append: 'px; --slide-width: var(--video-carousel-card-width);'
  assign mobile_style = '--slideshow-gap: 16px; --slide-width: ' | append: mobile_card_size | append: '%;'

  assign desktop_slideshow_id = 'video-carousel-desktop-' | append: section.id

  # Carousel navigation - copied from review-cards' settings verbatim, but the nav arrows
  # here live in the header (see the comment block above) rather than overlaid on media, so
  # unlike review-cards, icons_style: 'progress' doesn't exclude them - only hide_arrows and
  # icons_style: 'none' do.
  assign icons_style = section.settings.icons_style | default: 'progress'
  assign desktop_has_controls = false
  if card_count > columns
    assign desktop_has_controls = true
  endif
  assign mobile_has_controls = false
  if card_count > 1
    assign mobile_has_controls = true
  endif

  assign show_header_arrows = false
  if desktop_has_controls and icons_style != 'none' and section.settings.hide_arrows != true
    assign show_header_arrows = true
  endif

  assign icon_name = 'arrow'
  if icons_style contains 'chevron'
    assign icon_name = 'caret'
  endif

  assign desktop_gutters = null
  if bleed_right
    assign desktop_gutters = 'start'
  endif

  assign desktop_slideshow_attributes = 'id="' | append: desktop_slideshow_id | append: '"'

  # Same shared-card-width fix as sections/product-rail-tabs.liquid, but columns/card_gap
  # are dynamic settings here (2-6 / 12-40px) rather than fixed 4/24, so the formula is
  # built with Liquid instead of living as a static custom property in the stylesheet.
  # --video-carousel-card-width itself (below, on the .video-carousel div's style attribute)
  # is deliberately NOT built from the theme's --full-page-grid-central-column-width /
  # --util-page-margin-offset (assets/base.css) - those measured unreliably (a real 274px
  # instead of 294px at 1440, verified via getComputedStyle probes on sections/product-rail-
  # tabs.liquid) once read through a nested var()-in-calc() chain and finally consumed by
  # grid-template-columns on a box nested deep inside a force-full-width ancestor, rather
  # than the element .section itself declares them on. --page-content-width and --page-
  # margin, by contrast, are themselves plain fixed lengths with no `%` in their own
  # definitions (rem constants / max() of px values - .section--narrow further overrides
  # --page-content-width to a fixed 78rem in assets/custom.css), so rebuilding the same
  # min(content-width, viewport-minus-margins) clamp from THOSE plus 100vw measured
  # correctly everywhere it was tried.
  assign column_gap_span = columns | minus: 1 | times: card_gap
-%}

<div
  class="section-background{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
></div>

<div
  class="
    section
    section--{{ section.settings.section_width }}
    {% if section.settings.background_color != blank %}color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}
    video-carousel
    spacing-style
    {{ section.settings.css_class }}
  "
  style="
    {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
    --video-carousel-heading-color: {{ settings.color_palette.foreground }};
    --video-carousel-accent-color: {{ settings.color_palette.color4 }};
    --video-carousel-line-color: {{ settings.color_palette.color3 }};
    --video-tile-accent-color: {{ settings.color_palette.color4 }};
    --video-tile-chip-bg: {{ settings.color_palette.foreground | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.78 }};
    --video-carousel-card-width: calc((min(var(--page-content-width), calc(100vw - (2 * var(--page-margin)))) - {{ column_gap_span }}px) / {{ columns }});
  "
  data-testid="video-carousel"
>
  <div class="video-carousel__header">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="video-carousel__heading h2">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_header_arrows -%}
      <div class="video-carousel__nav hidden--mobile">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="video-carousel__nav-arrow video-carousel__nav-arrow--previous flip-x"
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.slideshow_previous' | t }}"
          on:click="#{{ desktop_slideshow_id }}/previous"
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper icon-{{ icon_name }}" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- if icon_name == 'caret' -%}
              {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="video-carousel__nav-arrow video-carousel__nav-arrow--next"
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.slideshow_next' | t }}"
          on:click="#{{ desktop_slideshow_id }}/next"
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper icon-{{ icon_name }}" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- if icon_name == 'caret' -%}
              {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if is_desktop_grid -%}
    <div
      class="video-carousel__desktop-grid hidden--mobile"
      style="--video-carousel-grid-columns: {{ columns }}; --video-carousel-grid-gap: {{ card_gap }}px;"
    >
      {{ desktop_grid_items }}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div
      class="video-carousel__desktop hidden--mobile{% if bleed_right %} force-full-width{% endif %}"
      style="{% if bleed_right %}--gutter-slide-width: var(--util-page-margin-offset);{% endif %}"
    >
      {%- capture desktop_controls -%}
        {%- if desktop_has_controls -%}
          {%- if section.settings.enable_dots -%}
            {%- render 'slideshow-controls',
              style: 'dots',
              autoplay: section.settings.autoplay,
              item_count: card_count,
              show_arrows: false,
              arrows_on_media: false,
              controls_on_media: false,
              pagination_position: 'center',
              class: 'video-carousel__controls'
            -%}
          {%- elsif icons_style == 'progress' -%}
            {%- render 'slideshow-controls',
              style: 'progress',
              item_count: card_count,
              show_arrows: false,
              arrows_on_media: false,
              controls_on_media: false,
              pagination_position: 'center',
              class: 'video-carousel__controls carousel-controls carousel-controls--progress'
            -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- render 'slideshow',
        ref: 'videoCarouselDesktop',
        class: 'video-carousel__slideshow',
        style: desktop_style,
        slides: desktop_slides,
        show_arrows: false,
        autoplay: section.settings.autoplay,
        autoplay_speed: section.settings.autoplay_speed,
        auto_hide_controls: false,
        infinite: false,
        initial_slide: 0,
        slide_count: card_count,
        slideshow_gutters: desktop_gutters,
        attributes: desktop_slideshow_attributes,
        controls: desktop_controls
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div
    class="video-carousel__mobile hidden--desktop force-full-width"
    style="--gutter-slide-width: var(--util-page-margin-offset);"
  >
    {%- capture mobile_controls -%}
      {%- if mobile_has_controls -%}
        {%- if section.settings.enable_dots -%}
          {%- render 'slideshow-controls',
            style: 'dots',
            autoplay: section.settings.autoplay,
            item_count: card_count,
            show_arrows: false,
            arrows_on_media: false,
            controls_on_media: false,
            pagination_position: 'center',
            class: 'video-carousel__controls'
          -%}
        {%- elsif icons_style == 'progress' -%}
          {%- render 'slideshow-controls',
            style: 'progress',
            item_count: card_count,
            show_arrows: false,
            arrows_on_media: false,
            controls_on_media: false,
            pagination_position: 'center',
            class: 'video-carousel__controls carousel-controls carousel-controls--progress'
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- render 'slideshow',
      ref: 'videoCarouselMobile',
      class: 'video-carousel__slideshow video-carousel__slideshow--mobile',
      style: mobile_style,
      slides: mobile_slides,
      show_arrows: false,
      autoplay: section.settings.autoplay,
      autoplay_speed: section.settings.autoplay_speed,
      auto_hide_controls: false,
      infinite: false,
      initial_slide: 0,
      slide_count: card_count,
      slideshow_gutters: 'start end',
      controls: mobile_controls
    -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .video-carousel__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-block-end: 28px;
  }

  .video-carousel__heading {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--video-carousel-heading-color, currentcolor);
  }

  .video-carousel__nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .video-carousel__nav-arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--video-carousel-line-color, #e0dcd2);
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--video-carousel-accent-color, #4a6a1d);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 180ms var(--animation-easing, ease), color 180ms var(--animation-easing, ease);
  }

  .video-carousel__nav-arrow:hover {
    background: var(--video-carousel-accent-color, #4a6a1d);
    color: var(--color-background, #fff);
  }

  .video-carousel__nav-arrow .svg-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
  }

  .video-carousel__nav-arrow svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .video-carousel__nav-arrow .icon-caret svg {
    rotate: -90deg;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .video-carousel .video-carousel__header .video-carousel__heading {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }

  /* Desktop: each slide is one tile, sized to 1/columns of the row - see --slide-width above. */
  .video-carousel__slide {
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  .video-carousel__desktop .video-carousel__slide {
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Desktop grid: when the tile count fits within `columns` (see is_desktop_grid in the
     Liquid above, default desktop_layout: 'auto') the row renders this contained grid
     instead of the force-full-width carousel above - with exactly `columns` tiles the
     carousel has nothing to scroll to, so bleed_right's right-edge bleed only clips the
     last tile against the viewport instead of genuinely peeking past it. This block is
     never force-full-width regardless of the bleed_right setting (bleed only makes sense
     once there's real overflow to scroll into), so it needs no --gutter-slide-width either
     - it sits in the section's normal content column, same as the heading above it. Column
     count comes from the section's own `columns` setting (2-6, unlike product-rail-tabs's
     fixed 4), set as an inline custom property. Track size is `--video-carousel-card-width`
     (set on the outer .video-carousel div, same value the carousel's --slide-width uses
     above) rather than `1fr`, so a tile is the exact same rendered width whichever branch
     is showing - `1fr` happened to compute the same number today (this grid's own box is
     exactly the content column width), but only the shared variable actually guarantees
     they can't drift apart again, the same fix as product-rail-tabs's grid track. */
  .video-carousel__desktop-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--video-carousel-grid-columns, 4), var(--video-carousel-card-width));
    gap: var(--video-carousel-grid-gap, 24px);
  }

  /* Progress bar / dots: contained to the content column even when the desktop row bleeds
     (force-full-width) - reset the global inset here, then re-apply it only in the two
     full-width contexts (mobile is always full-width; desktop only when bleed_right is on). */
  .video-carousel .slideshow-controls__progress {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-inline: 0;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .video-carousel .slideshow-controls__progress-track {
    height: 4px;
    background: var(--video-carousel-line-color, var(--color-border));
  }

  .video-carousel .slideshow-controls__progress-bar {
    background: var(--video-carousel-accent-color, var(--color-foreground));
  }

  /* The nav arrows live in the header only - always hide the progress style's own built-in
     arrows so they never double up next to the track. */
  .video-carousel .slideshow-controls__progress-arrows {
    display: none;
  }

  .video-carousel__mobile.force-full-width .slideshow-controls__progress,
  .video-carousel__desktop.force-full-width .slideshow-controls__progress {
    padding-inline: var(--util-page-margin-offset, var(--page-margin, 16px));
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.video_carousel",
  "class": "ui-test-video-carousel",
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "video_tile",
      "name": "t:names.video",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "video",
          "id": "video",
          "label": "t:settings.video"
        },
        {
          "type": "video_url",
          "id": "video_url",
          "label": "t:settings.video_external_url",
          "info": "t:info.video_external",
          "accept": ["youtube", "vimeo"],
          "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.video == blank }}"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "poster",
          "label": "t:settings.cover_image"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "duration",
          "label": "t:settings.duration",
          "placeholder": "0:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "alt",
          "label": "t:settings.video_alt_text",
          "info": "t:info.video_alt_text",
          "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.video == blank }}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header",
      "footer"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:settings.heading",
      "default": "More than 10,000 happy customers"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns",
      "label": "t:settings.columns",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_gap",
      "label": "t:settings.gap",
      "min": 12,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "t:settings.image_ratio",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "portrait",
          "label": "t:options.portrait"
        },
        {
          "value": "vertical",
          "label": "t:options.vertical"
        },
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "t:options.square"
        }
      ],
      "default": "portrait"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_radius",
      "label": "t:settings.card_radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_card_size",
      "label": "t:settings.mobile_card_size",
      "min": 50,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 70
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "bleed_right",
      "label": "t:settings.bleed_right",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "desktop_layout",
      "label": "t:settings.layout_type",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "auto",
          "label": "t:options.auto"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:options.carousel"
        }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.carousel_navigation"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_dots",
      "label": "Enable dots",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "hide_arrows",
      "label": "Hide arrows",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.enable_dots == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "autoplay",
      "label": "t:settings.auto_rotate_slides",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "autoplay_speed",
      "label": "t:settings.speed",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 7,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "s",
      "default": 4,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.autoplay == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
